---
import ShoreStations from "../tab-content/coastal-conditions-shore-stations.mdx";
import SubsurfaceMoorings from "../tab-content/coastal-conditions-subsurface-moorings.mdx";

const tabs = [
  {
    id: "surface-shore-stations",
    route: "coastal-temperatures/shore-stations",
    label: "Surface - Shore Stations",
    Content: ShoreStations
  },
  {
    id: "subsurface-moorings",
    route: "coastal-temperatures/subsurface-moorings",
    label: "Subsurface - Moorings",
    Content: SubsurfaceMoorings
  }
];
---

<section aria-label="Coastal temperature observations">
  <div class="hs-accordion-group mb-6">
    <div class="hs-accordion active overview-card" id="coastal-temperatures-key-messages">
      <header class="hs-accordion-heading overview-card__header">
        <button
          class="hs-accordion-toggle hs-accordion-active:text-primary-active inline-flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-x-3 text-start hover:text-muted-foreground-1 focus:outline-hidden focus:text-muted-foreground-1"
          aria-expanded="true"
          aria-controls="coastal-temperatures-key-messages-content"
        >
          <span class="overview-card__title" id="coastal-temperatures-key-messages-heading">Key messages</span>
          <svg class="hs-accordion-active:hidden block size-3.5" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M5 12h14" />
            <path d="M12 5v14" />
          </svg>
          <svg class="hs-accordion-active:block hidden size-3.5" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M5 12h14" />
          </svg>
        </button>
      </header>
      <div
        id="coastal-temperatures-key-messages-content"
        class="hs-accordion-content w-full overflow-hidden transition-[height] duration-300"
        role="region"
        aria-labelledby="coastal-temperatures-key-messages-heading"
      >
        <div class="overview-card__content text-muted-foreground">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm italic text-muted-foreground">Updated: November 18, 2026</p>
          <ul class="overview-card__list">
            <li><strong class="text-foreground">California’s coastal waters are at or near record warmth from San Diego to the Farallones.</strong> Scripps Pier is about 6 °C (11 °F) above its long-term average for mid-November. Southeast Farallon Island, 26 miles west of the Golden Gate, is about 5 °C (10 °F) above average.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-foreground">Scripps Pier has set 73 daily high-temperature records in 2026.</strong> On Nov 11 the pier measured 24.1 °C (75.4 °F) at both the surface and the bottom (about 5 m). Normally the water there is near 17–18 °C at this time of year. The <a href="https://shorestations.ucsd.edu/">pier’s record</a> goes back to 1916. Water this warm all the way to the bottom means no cold, nutrient-rich water is welling up near shore.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-foreground">Below the surface, El Niño is unmistakable in Central and Northern California.</strong> The M1 mooring in Monterey Bay recorded 19.22 °C at 60 m on Nov 10, the warmest in its roughly 35-year record and about 8 °C above normal. Off Trinidad Head, gliders found water up to 3–4 °C warmer than normal at 40–60 m. Warming at depth is the signature of El Niño heat moving north along the coast from the tropics.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-foreground">Northern California warmed sharply in late October-November.</strong> Sea surface temperature at the Trinidad Bay shore station, sampled by hand from the Trinidad pier, rose sharply in early November. It went from about 12.5 °C at the start of the month to more than 14 °C by November 7, then kept climbing to about 16.4 °C (61.5 °F) on November 14. That is roughly 4.5 °C above the long-term average for mid-November. The station has set 16 daily records so far in 2026, about half of them since November 8, in a record that goes back to 1973. The warming reached Trinidad about one to two weeks after the late-October jumps at MBARI’s M1 mooring, which suggests that El Niño–related warming is spreading north along the coast.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-foreground">Expect warm water to persist through winter and spring.</strong> El Niño’s coastal effects usually peak in winter and spring. Warm water also raises sea level, which adds to king tides (Nov 23–27, Dec 24–25) and winter storm surge.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="border-b border-line-2">
    <nav
      class="flex gap-x-1 overflow-x-auto overflow-y-hidden"
      aria-label="Coastal temperature observation types"
      role="tablist"
      aria-orientation="horizontal"
    >
      {
        tabs.map((tab, index) => (
          <button
            type="button"
            class:list={[
              "hs-tab-active:bg-layer hs-tab-active:border-b-transparent hs-tab-active:text-primary-active -mb-px inline-flex items-center gap-x-2 rounded-t-lg border border-line-2 bg-muted px-4 py-3 text-center text-sm font-medium text-muted-foreground-1 hover:text-foreground focus:outline-hidden focus:text-foreground disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50",
              index === 0 && "active"
            ]}
            id={`coastal-temperatures-${tab.id}-tab`}
            data-tab-route={tab.route}
            aria-selected={index === 0 ? "true" : "false"}
            data-hs-tab={`#coastal-temperatures-${tab.id}-panel`}
            aria-controls={`coastal-temperatures-${tab.id}-panel`}
            role="tab"
          >
            {tab.label}
          </button>
        ))
      }
    </nav>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-3">
    {
      tabs.map(({ id, Content }, index) => (
        <div
          id={`coastal-temperatures-${id}-panel`}
          class:list={[index !== 0 && "hidden"]}
          role="tabpanel"
          aria-labelledby={`coastal-temperatures-${id}-tab`}
        >
          <Content />
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>
